// EventsClean() – deduplicate by event_id and add a minute column.
//
// Coordinate rule: x,y are in the frame of the team IN POSSESSION (attacking
// towards x=105). Defensive events (pressure, tackle, interception) are
// recorded in the possessing team's frame, so "opponent half" for the
// defending team means x < 52.5.
//
// De-duplication: Eventstream may deliver the same event more than once.
// arg_max(EventEnqueuedUtcTime, *) keeps the most recently enqueued copy per
// event_id, matching the Python analytics.metrics._dedup() behaviour.

.create-or-alter function with (folder="whatif") EventsClean() {
    events
    | extend event_time = todatetime(event_time)
    | summarize arg_max(EventEnqueuedUtcTime, *) by event_id
    | extend minute = match_clock_s / 60
}

// Example: EventsClean() | take 5
